  "text": ">\";\n\nAssistant: Let's consider the determinant:\\\n\n\\[\n\\begin{vmatrix}\n\\cos^2 \\alpha & \\cos \\alpha \\sin \\alpha & \\sin^2 \\alpha \\\\\n\\cos^2 \\beta & \\cos \\beta \\sin \\beta & \\sin^2 \\beta \\\\\n\\cos^2 \\gamma & \\cos \\gamma \\sin \\gamma & \\sin^2 \\gamma\n\\end{vmatrix}\n\\]\n\nGiven that \\(\\alpha + \\beta + \\gamma = \\pi\\), we need to find the value of this determinant.\n\n**Step 1: Recognize the structure**\n The determinant can be expressed as a sum of the same determinants, which simplifies the problem.\n\\[\n\\begin{vmatrix}\n\\cos^2 \\alpha & \\cos \\alpha \\sin \\alpha & \\sin^2 \\alpha \\\\\n\\cos^2 \\beta & \\cos \\beta \\sin \\beta & \\sin^2 \\beta \\\\\n\\cos^2 \\gamma & \\cos \\gamma \\sin \\gamma & \\sin^2 \\gamma\n\\end{vmatrix}\n=\n\\cos^2 \\alpha \\cross \\sin^2 \\beta + \\cos \\alpha \\sin \\alpha \\cross \\sin^2 \\gamma + \\sin^2 \\alpha \\cross \\cos^2 \\beta \\\\\n-\n\\cos \\alpha \\sin \\alpha \\cross \\cos^2 \\beta + \\sin^2 \\alpha \\cross \\sin^2 \\gamma + \\cos^2 \\alpha \\cross \\cos^2 \\beta\n\\]\n\n**Step 2: Simplify the expression**\n We simplify the determinant by subtracting and adding terms:\n\\[\n\\begin{vmatrix}\n\\cos^2 \\alpha & \\cos \\alpha \\sin \\alpha & \\sin^2 \\alpha \\\\\n\\cos^2 \\beta & \\cos \\beta \\sin \\beta & \\sin^2 \\beta \\\\\n\\cos^2 \\gamma & \\cos \\gamma \\sin \\gamma & \\sin^2 \\gamma\n\\end{vmatrix}\n=\n\\cos^2 \\alpha \\cross \\left( \\sin^2 \\beta - \\sin^2 \\gamma \\right) + \\cos \\alpha \\sin \\alpha \\cross \\left( \\left( \\sin^2 \\gamma - \\sin^2 \\beta \\right) + \\left( \\cos^2 \\gamma - \\cos^2 \\beta \\right) \\right) + \\sin^2 \\alpha \\cross \\left( \\sin^2 \\beta - \\sin^2 \\gamma \\right) \\\\\n-\n\\cos \\alpha \\sin \\alpha \\cross \\left( \\cos^2 \\beta - \\sin^2 \\gamma \\right) + \\sin^2 \\alpha \\cross \\left( \\cos^2 \\gamma - \\sin^2 \\beta \\right) + \\cos^2 \\alpha \\cross \\left( \\sin^2 \\beta - \\sin^2 \\gamma \\right)\n\\]\n\n**Step 3: Simplify using triginometric properties**\n Using the property \\(\\sin\\beta\\sin\\gamma = \\cos(\\alpha+\\beta+\\gamma)\\), we have:\n\\[\n\\sin^2 \\alpha \\cross \\left( \\sin^2 \\beta - \\sin^2 \\gamma \\right) = \\sin^2 \\alpha \\cross \\left( -2 \\cos(2 \\alpha + \\pi / 2) \\left( \\cos^2 \\beta - \\cos^2 \\gamma \\right) \\right)\n\\]\n\\[\n\\sin^2 \\alpha \\cross \\left( -2 \\cos(2 \\alpha + \\pi / 2) \\left( \\cos^2 \\beta - \\cos^2 \\gamma \\right) \\right) = \\sin^2 \\alpha \\cross \\left(2 \\cos(2 \\alpha + \\pi / 2) \\left( \\cos^2 \\beta - \\cos^2 \\gamma \\right) \\right)\n\\]\n\nHence, the determinant simplifies to:\n\\[\n2 \\cdot \\left( \\sin^2 \\alpha \\left( \\cos^2 \\beta - \\cos^2 \\gamma \\right) \\right)\n\\]\n\nThis completes the final step of the calculations.\n\n**Answer:**\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{1}\n\\]",
